### Rust ###
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed: this crate builds an executable
# (the `noveum-ai-gateway` binary and the Cloudflare Worker), so the lockfile is
# part of the build input. The Dockerfile does `COPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock ./`,
# which means ignoring it breaks `docker build` on a fresh clone. It also gives
# CI reproducible builds and lets `cargo audit`/`cargo deny` see the real tree.
# https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# End of https://www.toptal.com/developers/gitignore/api/rust
Apollo

build/
.wrangler/
node_modules/
